! C2H7O3Cl | caa005bTSb: TRANSITION STATE at wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water)
!
! Part of the same 3-point refinement as caa007a/caa007b (first/last IRC
! points), this one for the TS. Starting geometry is the converged saddle
! point from caa005bTSa.log ("***** SADDLE POINT LOCATED *****"), which
! was itself confirmed genuine at the original level (wB97X-D, GBASIS=N21
! NGAUSS=6 NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.T., i.e. a 3-21G-family basis with diffuse and
! polarization functions, not the same as the IRC path's 6-31G(d)-style
! basis, but same functional): EXACTLY ONE imaginary frequency (1156.17i),
! all other modes real. That original search used an explicitly supplied
! starting Hessian ($HESS ... READ). We do not have an equivalent Hessian
! for this new basis, so this run instead relies on IHREP=1 (a genuinely
! fresh Hessian recomputed every step) plus GAMESS's default mode-following
! (IFOLOW=1) to track the correct transition mode -- the same approach that
! has already worked reliably for caa007a/caa007b's minimizations.
!
! RUNTYP=SADPOINT (NOT OPTIMIZE) -- this searches for a first-order saddle
! point rather than a minimum, essential for a TS. Using OPTIMIZE here
! would simply relax the structure down into a nearby minimum, losing the
! transition state entirely.
!
! NOTE: first submission attempt omitted an explicit HESS= setting in
! $STATPT. Unlike RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE (which defaults to HESS=GUESS),
! RUNTYP=SADPOINT defaults to HESS=READ, expecting an explicit $HESS group
! -- which we don't have for this basis. GAMESS aborted immediately with
! "YOU DID NOT SUPPLY A $HESS GROUP." Fixed by explicitly setting
! HESS=GUESS, overriding that default; IHREP=1 (fresh Hessian every step)
! should correct for the guess's lower quality quickly, the same way it
! did for caa007a/caa007b's minimizations.
!
! NOTE (final): switched strategy entirely rather than keep fighting the
! HESS=GUESS override (see caa005bTSb-hess.inp). Computed a genuine Hessian
! via a standalone RUNTYP=HESSIAN run at this exact geometry/level, then
! extracted the PROJECTED Hessian block (translation/rotation removed,
! matching PROJCT=.T.) from caa005bTSb-hess.dat -- confirmed by the
! "----- HESSIAN MATRIX AFTER PROJECTION -----" label immediately preceding
! it in the punch file, distinguishing it from the earlier raw/unprojected
! $HESS block. That block is appended below and HESS is set to READ
! (GAMESS's own default for SADPOINT), working with the program rather
! than against it.
!
! NOTE (correction): using the pre-projected Hessian caused a NEW error --
! "NOT 5 OR 6 TRANS/ROT MODES, NUM T/R=7" -- one spurious extra near-zero
! eigenvalue beyond the expected 6, most likely from this run's own
! PROJCT=.T. re-projecting an already-projected Hessian (double
! projection). Checked directly in GAMESS's source (statpt.src): the
! trans/rot count comes from counting eigenvalues below a small tolerance
! (TRTOL), and the check (hardcoded N5OR6=5, tolerating up to N5OR6+1=6
! total) rejected our 7. Fixed by using the RAW (unprojected) $HESS block
! instead, letting THIS run's own PROJCT=.T. do the projection exactly
! once, consistently -- the standard way HESS=READ is normally used.
!
! Everything else identical to caa007a/caa007b: wB97X-D, PCM(water), native
! GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 (6-31G(d,p)), DXMAX=0.02, Cartesian
! coordinates, METHOD=SEMINUM (wB97X-D has no analytic Hessian regardless
! of basis).

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=SADPOINT DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.0001 NSTEP=300 IHREP=1 HESS=READ
         HSSEND=.T. DXMAX=0.02 NPRT=1 $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.F. AUTO=.F. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PROJCT=.T. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=100 MEMDDI=200 $END

 $DATA
Chloroacetaldehyde hydrate and water -- TS, re-search at 6-31G(d,p)
